Third-party acknowledgments
===========================

The MIT License above covers YouRec’s original source code and documentation.
Salvatore Sanfilippo reserves rights to the YouRec name and icon as branding.
The following works retain their own licenses and copyright notices. Full texts,
upstream revisions, file locations, and conversion records are indexed in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and included with the app under Credits.

Audio restoration
-----------------
* RNNoise v0.1 and its pretrained network, by Jean-Marc Valin, Mozilla and the
  Xiph.Org contributors: BSD 3-Clause. Its CELT/Opus, libogg, KISS FFT (Mark
  Borgerding) and network component notices include BSD 2-Clause terms. See
  ThirdParty/RNNoise/COPYING, the original source headers and the bundled notices.
* DeepFilterNet3 model and DSP data, by Hendrik Schröter and contributors: MIT.
  Kyle Howells’ DeepFilterNet-mlx streaming implementation and conversion:
  MIT or Apache License 2.0. See ThirdParty/DeepFilterNet3.
* LavaSR v2 by Yatharth Sharma: Apache License 2.0. Its Vocos architecture
  by Hubert Siuzdak and Charactr Inc. is MIT-licensed. The model was converted
  to Core ML. See ThirdParty/LavaSR and https://github.com/gemelo-ai/vocos.
* VoiceFixer architecture and code by Haohe Liu and contributors: MIT.
  Haohe Liu’s VoiceFixer Model CheckPoint v3 and the adapted weights are
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). YouRec converts
  the model to Core ML and implements fixed-window inference and overlap
  blending. Checkpoints: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5600188
  License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Sources and conversion notes: ThirdParty/VoiceFixer/PROVENANCE.md.

Subtitles and libraries
-----------------------
* Qwen3-ASR-0.6B by the Qwen team and aufklarer’s MLX 4-bit conversion and
  tokenizer: Apache License 2.0. These assets download on demand. YouRec uses
  a modified subset of Soniqo’s speech-swift (Apache License 2.0).
  See ThirdParty/QwenASR/PROVENANCE.md.
* Apple’s MLX, MLX C and MLX Swift: MIT. Apple metal-cpp: Apache License 2.0.
  fmt by Victor Zverovich and contributors: MIT. JSON for Modern C++ by Niels
  Lohmann and contributors: MIT, with embedded notices including an Apache 2.0
  contribution. PocketFFT by Martin Reinecke and Peter Bell: BSD 3-Clause.
  Norbert Juffa’s Metal exponential routine: BSD 2-Clause. Swift Numerics by
  Apple and contributors: Apache License 2.0 with Runtime Library Exception.
  See ThirdParty/QwenASR/DEPENDENCY-LICENSES.txt and YouRec/ThirdPartyNotices.txt.
* ZIPFoundation by Thomas Zoechling and contributors: MIT.
  See ThirdParty/ZIPFoundation/LICENSE.

Fonts, images and platform
--------------------------
* Archivo Black, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, Barlow Condensed, Caveat, Fraunces,
  IBM Plex Mono and Source Serif 4, distributed through Google Fonts: SIL Open
  Font License 1.1. Each family's original copyright and license are preserved in
  ThirdParty/TitleFonts/<family>/OFL.txt.
* The test portrait of Eileen Collins is a public-domain NASA photograph obtained
  from the scikit-image sample dataset. See Tests/Fixtures/README.md.
* Apple system frameworks, the Apple SDK and SF Symbols are used under Apple's
  applicable platform and SF Symbols terms: https://developer.apple.com/support/terms/
  and https://developer.apple.com/sf-symbols/.

Development tools (run separately from the iPhone app)
-----------------------------------------------------
Model conversion uses PyTorch, coremltools, NumPy and SciPy (BSD 3-Clause),
torchaudio (BSD 2-Clause), torchlibrosa and PyYAML (MIT), librosa (ISC),
Python SoundFile (BSD 3-Clause), Matplotlib (Matplotlib license) and progressbar
(BSD or LGPL 2.1 or later). Test and research tools include OpenCV 4 (Apache 2.0),
PyAV (BSD 3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU), FFmpeg (LGPL 2.1 or later, or GPL
depending on build configuration), and the FastDVDnet research baseline by
Matias Tassano and collaborators (MIT). Release automation uses Xcode (Apple
SDK terms) and the App Store Connect CLI by Rudrank Riyam and contributors
(MIT, https://github.com/rudrankriyam/App-Store-Connect-CLI).
